<decompilertest>
<!--
    callpopret: flow a `call` through a callee that pops the pushed return
    address off the stack and `ret`s through the word above it.

    CALL is a fall-through op, so kuna decodes the return address as the next
    instruction.  The oldest position-independent idiom on x86 breaks that by
    calling over its own inline data: the callee pops the pushed return address,
    steps past a pad byte and `ret`s, so control returns to the CALLER'S caller
    with a pointer to the data in a register.  The return address is never
    reached and the bytes after the call are not instructions.
    Stage model: S2 flow classification (`xref_control_flow`, the CPUI_CALL arm).

    Layout (linked flat, x86-32):
      caller @ 0x100000 : call 0x100010      ; return address is 0x100005
                 0x100005 : 90               ; pad - control never arrives here
                 0x100006 : 6c 6c c3         ; DATA - the pointer the helper returns
      getptr @ 0x100010 : pop eax            ; EAX = 0x100005
                 0x100011 : inc eax          ; step past the pad -> 0x100006
                 0x100012 : ret              ; return to caller's OWN caller

    Decoded as a fall-through the data lifts as instructions: `6c` is INSB, so
    the body fills with port reads the program never performs, and the pointer
    the helper exists to hand back appears nowhere.

    Pass 1 (callpopret off, the bug): the fall-through at 0x100005 is decoded and
    the port reads appear.
    Pass 2 (default, callpopret on): the call is followed as a branch, the pop
    and the `ret` join the caller, and the body is `return 0x100006`.

    Assert #1 pins the recovered pointer to EXACTLY ONE occurrence across both
    print C passes: present in the default pass, absent in the callpopret-off
    one.  Assert #2 pins the two port reads the other way round (both bytes of
    the data decode as INSB), so the fix has to RESTORE the pointer and not
    merely stop emitting junk.
-->
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:gcc">
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">e80b000000906c6cc3</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100010" readonly="true">5840c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="caller"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option callpopret off</com>
  <com>lo fu caller</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option callpopret on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CALLPOPRET #1: the default pass follows the call as a branch and recovers the pointer to the inline data" min="1" max="1">return 0x100006;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLPOPRET #2: the two port reads decoded at the unreachable return address appear only in the callpopret-off pass" min="2" max="2">in\(</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
